From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Callaghan <johnocallaghan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:25:10 +0100
Subject: media: meson: vdec: start MPEG-1/2 only when CAPTURE streams

MPEG-1/2 reads its CAPTURE buffers once, when the decoder starts.
GStreamer starts the OUTPUT queue first, so no CAPTURE buffer exists yet.
The firmware then writes every picture to canvas 0.
On G12A, canvas 0 is the console framebuffer. Decoding also stalls.

Wait for the CAPTURE queue before the start, as before 876f123b8956.

Fixes: 876f123b8956 ("media: meson: vdec: bring up to compliance")
Assisted-by: Claude
Signed-off-by: John O'Callaghan <johnocallaghan@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c | 21 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/vdec.c
@@ -259,6 +259,23 @@ static int vdec_queue_setup(struct vb2_queue *q, unsigned int *num_buffers,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The session starts once the OUTPUT queue is streaming. Codecs without
+ * dynamic resolution support (MPEG-1/2) program the canvases of the queued
+ * CAPTURE buffers when they start, so for them the CAPTURE queue has to be
+ * streaming as well.
+ */
+static bool vdec_can_start(struct amvdec_session *sess)
+{
+	if (!sess->streamon_out)
+		return false;
+
+	if (!(sess->fmt_out->flags & V4L2_FMT_FLAG_DYN_RESOLUTION))
+		return sess->streamon_cap;
+
+	return true;
+}
+
 static void vdec_vb2_buf_queue(struct vb2_buffer *vb)
 {
 	struct vb2_v4l2_buffer *vbuf = to_vb2_v4l2_buffer(vb);
@@ -267,7 +284,7 @@ static void vdec_vb2_buf_queue(struct vb2_buffer *vb)
 
 	v4l2_m2m_buf_queue(m2m_ctx, vbuf);
 
-	if (!sess->streamon_out)
+	if (!vdec_can_start(sess))
 		return;
 
 	if (sess->streamon_cap &&
@@ -296,7 +313,7 @@ static int vdec_start_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q, unsigned int count)
 	else
 		sess->streamon_cap = 1;
 
-	if (!sess->streamon_out)
+	if (!vdec_can_start(sess))
 		return 0;
 
 	if (sess->status == STATUS_NEEDS_RESUME &&
